":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5014006","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1b4a0c95051bfe59ce2bfd52b43481f7c4f0a88c086aadf767131bb72beab2ab","compact":"d537464e2b9b131645c13ce1223baaf7e0ebcc7d5e976f36f802de908b696a24","nasal":"91d0db3b177f0ab6aa83a921d093bca8d47d23307286bb350f19fab7135c5a86"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-14-7","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":14,"verse":7,"english":"For this (damsel) was killed the mighty Vāli and Kabandha-Rāvana's equal in prowess.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-16-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5014007","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bf8879255f001a7d1db960c4fe0e9a2f1fd5504aa41e52b7e276fae8439f9e12","compact":"7945550c318ce5adf9ae8cd9117095747a9e25327c025970ef114ef4c243a9a3","nasal":"91555689070b987ca78cb8b3460fa29877ac3cf67f0ae2964b040416085f7477"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-14-8","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":14,"verse":8,"english":"For her (too) was destroyed in battle, the terribly powerful Rākşasa-Viradha, by Rāma putting forth his energy, like to ſambara killed by Mahendra.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-16-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5014008","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0377727cc953d0b2b5e6a84f436c4247d2b7ce4e81c682ff89ed2ab1c071455c","compact":"637405c2c7f7061a797f2fac12c873c934e37ecc08a55861dd4e58870f20c264","nasal":"d46765f5691317019fa1fcd151db639e111c7ab25c2584a1dcde189b8eedeab5"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-14-9","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":14,"verse":9,"english":"(It was for her) that fourteen thousand Rākşasas of terrible deeds were destroyed at Janasthāna with arrow resembling the flame of fire. And Khara was killed in battle, and Trisirā was discomfited and the mighty Dūşaņa by Rāma, knowing his ownself.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-16-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5014009","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"48363dc29774a58d8c713b03d299f6ffedef679bd52c1030d28d2795526a06d7","compact":"339eff5e399fced34e2d94ccb1f41e5e5064a399df4aade4a9f562b1987ae07c","nasal":"339eff5e399fced34e2d94ccb1f41e5e5064a399df4aade4a9f562b1987ae07c"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-14-10","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":14,"verse":10,"english":"(It was for her) that fourteen thousand Rākşasas of terrible deeds were destroyed at Janasthāna with arrow resembling the flame of fire. And Khara was killed in battle, and Trisirā was discomfited and the mighty Dūşaņa by Rāma, knowing his ownself.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-16-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5014010","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"140df71507a4acae26f8bc3e3818c999ce8fc7ffe23e5a7e26e527221288c2ca","compact":"6e07ea14a50e2c6ce96fc2202f2df2d50e7040934dc4bc714e68516a2960b215","nasal":"6e07ea14a50e2c6ce96fc2202f2df2d50e7040934dc4bc714e68516a2960b215"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-14-11","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":14,"verse":11,"english":"And it was on her account that Sugrīva, known all over the world, came by the wealth of the monkeys hard to acquire and amassed by Vali.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.833,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-16-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5014011","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e0968c2be163dce06068fbdd8ffc1b523388b9469a89e5be357206afaf51ece1","compact":"c8b3f5960da9e61cc75f34b618a8c088a756612e0e5d8184b55