,"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5014017","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fda3b075fd597f477423fb52c2f60eb86363afdcd561f410a1c6165e0de53553","compact":"9d43aae5ccc13a48eb72a1e6a8f35405d4a5c15388c54cf5ef397b1953e34a03","nasal":"00fa583f37f2c822fb00a29eeee06153d2131ad619a0b36a3d19334789fc22eb"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-14-18","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":14,"verse":18,"english":"And She is the beloved spouse of the pious and grateful Rāma, knowing his ownself, and has been brought under the control of the Raksasis.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-16-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5014018","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"29c75a88dcac326d44c28e74393531158c188e0be4467ef9aa82801306699324","compact":"2f1f64ed9f813886b26692647ccdbeb7b27b8ee52f615ee4109ba4482f0f7f39","nasal":"2f1f64ed9f813886b26692647ccdbeb7b27b8ee52f615ee4109ba4482f0f7f39"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-14-19","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":14,"verse":19,"english":"Renouncing all luxuries, and considering not the least about miseries, she actuated by her husband's love entered the solitary forest.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.849,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-16-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5014019","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f364e396a4856bc657dc0c5c98b87d9ec16410713ff6a27df1eaba19b5bea150","compact":"c6d8cc7e7e7ac5bdf3761a7070e0372ba39e0f150657695f6c4da9f07989ce96","nasal":"c3bea1483ca39c2ef7532d278b2f523b3f8a2f994701694e6a74893a7fc516a1"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-14-20","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":14,"verse":20,"english":"And satisfied with fruits and roots and ever engaged in her husband's service, she lived in the forest as much delighted as she was in her house.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.815,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-16-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5014020","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a1ccd9311e85491ea7b9a46d58a6cfa4bdc5bcdb4372c7f1d372983345eae1f9","compact":"9d1028d20ef513be1c74bf576b3f7dc0318c9f40b26018b5096056268647858e","nasal":"9d1028d20ef513be1c74bf576b3f7dc0318c9f40b26018b5096056268647858e"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-14-21","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":14,"verse":21,"english":"And that one of a golden hue, never used to afflictions and who was wont to converse always with a delighted countenance, has now been suffering incomparable miseries.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-16-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5014021","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"26c13176ddd923ff5a152185021d1a72059d1cf3434e58d53ee210bb5e161361","compact":"b35bb9451b24b3ed8edd8986ec11a70de6b0269c881f3cdd763cf4ce95eee24a","nasal":"d8e8b0f63ff29f837cdb8a04d5a0cffa7f10be9ab09161d263f6dfbdf0c08fa0"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-14-22","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":14,"verse":22,"english":"Like to a thirsty wight longing for an abode where he might get a drink, Rāghava pants after seeing her, gifted with an exalted character and oppressed by Rāvana.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-16-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5014022","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"89ec5bd5c30c429f57c0f8c0acb60ad441778b7935002b60aadc070bef0561de","compact":"210febe62a158ff0aadf4d8a35d7db5dc8d7f5348612ec32ac6756e54a0e81a6","nasal":"599b4062291b6baac0333b8d46ca4799fdde30067d58aa65ea26c0b4d233fed2"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-14-23","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":14,"verse":23,"english":"As a monarch who had lost his kingdom, is greatly delighted when he regain it, forsooth shall Rāghava, in like manner, be pleased when he shall come by her.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-16-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5014023","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3723078205e68bb501e93be37edf1e2fa5e51ada949b14c3680b65cbea3c1cd2","compact":"659a0cb4f7f0ea99b18ea08a237ce1e883206b475c38147468c2adb2f37168a0","nasal":"659a0cb4f7f0ea99b18ea08a237ce1e883206b475c38147468c2adb2f37168a0"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-14-24","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":14,"verse":24,"english":"She too has been maintaining her being in the hope of seeing Rāma again, separated as she is from her friends and deprived of all comforts and luxuries.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-16-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5014024","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c089636988e9b6556a06e358eb6b17def54f96893576abfc9649b2782fbf86c9","compact":"3a695344bfa8de6a4d8aa00d5ce4221daa64e6f874aa986b727a8a200f990b47","nasal":"e372b49c495dac8fb15da3df138257e7f2a97a5d874f68a086caeb02cb4069e9"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-14-25","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":14,"verse":25,"english":"These Rākşasīs, and these trees enveloped with fruits and flowers-forsooth she dose not behold, but is engaged with all her heart in medidations only touching Rāma.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.855,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-16-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5014025","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5aa4269f517f34209526570ebb4b732eb184868c9d